# RRF macro line length (255 characters)

RepRapFirmware rejects startup and macro lines longer than about **255 characters** (`GCode command too long`, often reported at column 256).

## Rules

- Keep every line in `macros/**/*.g` at **≤255 characters** (logical line, excluding `\n`).
- Long `if { ... }` conditions must be **split** (nested `if`, or set a `var` flag in steps) — do not rely on one giant boolean expression.
- Run **`./dist/check-macro-line-length.sh`** before committing macro changes; CI runs the same check on pull requests.

## Pattern (MOS import gate style)

```gcode
var nxtDoThing = false
if { fileexists("0:/sys/foo.requested") }
    set var.nxtDoThing = true
if { !var.nxtDoThing && fileexists("0:/sys/bar.g") }
    set var.nxtDoThing = true
if { var.nxtDoThing }
    M98 P"target.g"
```

## Anti-pattern

```gcode
; BAD — will fail at boot if over limit
if { fileexists("a") || fileexists("b") || exists(global.x) || exists(global.y) || ... }
```
